=== 09:29:52 gh issue create --repo dvystrcil/obico --title Add mid-print failure notification via Obico integration --body-file -
## Why
Obico's failure detection currently alerts only on print completion or explicit failure at start. Mid-print failures (e.g., filament runout, nozzle clog, power loss during print) are not surfaced as notifications, leaving prints unmonitored and potentially wasting material or causing damage.

## What we know
- Obico runs in the `obico` namespace with pods: `obico-web`, `obico-ml-api`, `obico-tasks`, `obico-postgres`, `obico-redis`. (Live pods)
- The `obico-docker-runner` and `obico-runner` pods handle listeners and secret scanning. (Live pods + obico repo files)
- Obico uses Moonraker/OctoPrint APIs to detect print state changes. (homelab/architecture docs imply Moonraker integration for 3D printer monitoring)
- No evidence of existing mid-print failure alerting logic in Obico manifests or workflows. (No matching code patterns found in obico repo files)

**unverified**: Exact Moonraker event names for mid-print failure states (e.g., `error`, `shutdown`, `pause`) and whether Obico exposes them via its API/webhook system.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** Configure Obico to emit webhook events on Moonraker `error`, `shutdown`, or `pause` states during active prints.
- [ ] **AC2.** Verify that a test mid-print failure (e.g., simulated filament runout via Klipper macro) triggers an email notification within 60 seconds.
- [ ] **AC3.** Confirm no false positives during normal print pauses/resumes (e.g., manual pause/unpause via Fluidd).

## Lane
claude — requires design decisions: which Moonraker events map to "mid-print failure", notification channel (email only, per Obico SMTP config), and whether to extend Obico's ML failure model or use raw Moonraker events directly.

